"""
The programme roxie, its command line declared with
Standard.Arguments:

    roxie                      the collector, a FastCGI responder behind
                               Hiawatha on the socket of --socket,
                               ROXIE_SOCKET or /run/roxie/roxie.sock
    roxie serve SOCKET         the same on the socket at SOCKET, an absolute path
                               of at most 100 bytes (a directory of its own, as
                               /run/roxie/roxie.sock)
    roxie allow NAME SUB       the account SUB of RAMBO signs in as the user
                               NAME
    roxie revoke-user NAME     no account of RAMBO signs in as NAME any more
    roxie token HOST           a token for the agent of HOST, shown once
    roxie revoke HOST          revokes the tokens of HOST
    roxie agent CONFIG         the agent: a round every few seconds until
                               SIGTERM or SIGINT
    roxie agent-once CONFIG    one round of the agent, then exit
    roxie prune DAYS           takes lines and samples older than DAYS days
                               out of the store, 1 to 36500
    roxie relevel              gives every kept line the level of today's
                               rules, beside the running collector

    roxie query QUERY...       the lines QUERY finds, newest first, as text
                               or with --json as JSON; --limit N, --since
                               SINCE (docs/syntax.md)
    roxie doctor               checks the files of the collector in the
                               working directory and its socket

and what Standard.Arguments builds in: -h, --help and help, -V, --version
and version (--full), info, -v, -s and sandbox, setup completion bash|zsh|
fish and setup manual, and for a word nearly right the word meant.

The collector works in its working directory: roxie.db, csrf.key,
pseudonym.key, audit.log, access.log, known-passwords.txt, and rambo.conf
and rambo-secret of the sign-in through RAMBO.
"""

module Roxie.App is
    """
    The programme.

    No contract: what it does is its exit status and its output, none a
    condition could check in O(1).
    """
    function main(root: RootCapability): ExitCode;
end module.
